# AEM Correctness Rules (prevent hallucination)

## Content Fragments
- Use: com.adobe.cq.dam.cfm.ContentFragment, FragmentTemplate,
  com.adobe.cq.dam.cfm.ContentFragmentManager
- Adapt: resource.adaptTo(ContentFragment.class)
- GraphQL is READ-ONLY in AEM — NEVER use it for create/update/delete
- CFM location: /conf/assessment/settings/dam/cfm/models
- Ticket content: /content/dam/assessment/tickets
- Comment content: /content/dam/assessment/comments

## Resource Resolution
- Use ResourceResolverFactory.getServiceResourceResolver(authInfo) with a system service user
- NEVER use admin resolver / getAdministrativeResourceResolver
- ALWAYS close ResourceResolver (try-with-resources)
- Service user subservice name: "assessment-service"

## Servlets
- Register via property "sling.servlet.paths=/bin/api/v1/..." (NOT resourceTypes)
- Read-only: extend SlingSafeMethodsServlet
- Writes: extend SlingAllMethodsServlet
- Always resp.setContentType("application/json"); set correct HTTP status

## Users
- Access via resolver.adaptTo(UserManager.class)
- Read profile props: profile/givenName, profile/familyName, profile/email
- Skip system users (isSystemUser())

## OSGi Config
- Place runtime configs in ui.config (org.apache.sling.serviceusermapping... for service user)

## If an API is uncertain
- State the assumption and cite the exact class/package; do NOT invent method names
